 "_design_r1": "Overlord dropkick startup (Fair, Big Band j.HK): f0 already breaks from the fall (knees up, arms lifting out), f1-f4 hard tuck (knees snap to the chest, arms thrown forward and wide, not twinned), f4-f11 the coil stays alive and rocks back, f12-f15 both legs shoot forward together (42% of the release on f14, 58% on f15 = first active frame), body lays back to near horizontal with a 28 deg barrel roll (left hip up) and 12 deg yaw so the legs read from behind, left arm flung overhead-back, right arm out-back-low, head curled up looking over the feet. f15 == loop f11.",
 "_changes": "k6 (2026-11-21, owner on the K5 r3 videos): ROUND 2: arms OPEN a3 (key 2), SLAM into the press a5 (key 4, chest curls 6, shoulders up), hold a6, RELEASE a8 (key 7, elbows out, shoulders down); key 8 removed. Round 1: re-keyed on the build frames; a4 arms PRESS into the fold (shoulders in, wrap deeper, chest curls), a8 relax a little, a11 gather; head lags the tuck at a4 and overshoots at a8; knees overshoot 2 cm at a8; a15 lying fold clamps. Previous: k5 (2026-11-21, owner on the r4 videos): arms snap crossed by f3 (Bison cross, forearms on the chest); tuck to a ball laid back by f7, chamber f11-f13, smear f14, strike f15 with legs locked and chin "
}